From 7a6171f80ef9a74a394460ae3c35caa9870f24c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 06:57:50 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Linux: Nintendo stream music, memory stick names in any case,
 a type fix

Three faults the native Linux build had that the Windows one does not:

- The bundled FFmpeg built on Linux and macOS (--disable-everything and a
  short list) had no BRSTM or BFSTM demuxer and no DSP-ADPCM decoder, so a
  port's .brstm/.bcstm/.bfstm music was left out as unreadable. Windows uses
  a full prebuilt LGPL build. Added brstm, bfstm, adpcm_thp, adpcm_thp_le.
- ms0: paths were looked up as the game wrote them. A memory stick and
  Windows match names in any case, and games rely on it: Dissidia 012 asks
  whether ".../2f356e6c.edat" exists, then opens ".../2F356E6C.EDAT", so its
  DLC music was silent on Linux. host_path() now matches each part of the
  path in any ASCII case off Windows; a part not found is kept as written.
- texture_pack_match.cpp: a {a, b} list mixed unsigned long long and
  std::uint64_t, which is unsigned long on Linux, and did not compile.

Checked on a Steam Deck (SteamOS, native build): a mod's 31 BRSTM tracks
are listed and play, and DLC tracks play.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 cmake/FFmpeg.cmake              |  9 +++++---
 host/gpu/texture_pack_match.cpp |  2 +-
 host/hle/hle_io.cpp             | 41 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 47 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cmake/FFmpeg.cmake b/cmake/FFmpeg.cmake
index 5fbfec5..cf3a35b 100644
--- a/cmake/FFmpeg.cmake
+++ b/cmake/FFmpeg.cmake
@@ -29,7 +29,10 @@ set(PORTABLEKIT_FFMPEG_SOVERSIONS avcodec 61 avutil 59 avformat 61 swresample 5)
 # whose movie streams the host splits into access units and whose pixels it
 # converts itself; and for host audio files the WAV, MP3, Ogg and FLAC
 # demuxers, their parsers, the MP3, Vorbis, Opus, FLAC and PCM decoders and the
-# resampler. Host files are read through the host's own I/O, so no protocol is
+# resampler; and the BRSTM and BFSTM demuxers (BFSTM's reads BCSTM too) with
+# their DSP-ADPCM decoders, for Nintendo stream files with their loops (the
+# Windows build's prebuilt FFmpeg has every format). Host files are read
+# through the host's own I/O, so no protocol is
 # built. No scaler, filter, device or network code. No GPL or non-free parts:
 # the result is LGPL-2.1-or-later, which the build checks.
 set(PORTABLEKIT_FFMPEG_CONFIGURE_FLAGS
@@ -43,8 +46,8 @@ set(PORTABLEKIT_FFMPEG_CONFIGURE_FLAGS
     --disable-network
     --disable-autodetect
     --disable-everything
-    --enable-decoder=atrac3,atrac3p,h264,mp3float,vorbis,opus,flac,pcm_s16le,pcm_s24le,pcm_s32le,pcm_f32le,pcm_u8
-    --enable-demuxer=wav,mp3,ogg,flac
+    --enable-decoder=atrac3,atrac3p,h264,mp3float,vorbis,opus,flac,pcm_s16le,pcm_s24le,pcm_s32le,pcm_f32le,pcm_u8,adpcm_thp,adpcm_thp_le
+    --enable-demuxer=wav,mp3,ogg,flac,brstm,bfstm
     --enable-parser=mpegaudio,vorbis,opus,flac
     --disable-x86asm
     --disable-debug)
